comment_body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If `asset_id` is `nullptr`, calling `native_assets_manager->LookupNativeAsset(asset_id)` will cause undefined behavior or a crash (since `LookupNativeAsset` likely expects a valid string/pointer). Although `NativeAssetIdForError` handles `nullptr` defensively in the error path, the crash will occur before any error is reported. Adding an explicit null check for `asset_id` before calling `LookupNativeAsset` ensures robust defensive programming.

```c
  if (asset_id == nullptr) {
    if (report_missing_assets) {
      SetNativeAssetUnavailableError(asset_id, native_assets_manager.get(),
                                     error);
    }
    return nullptr;
  }

  std::vector<std::string> asset_path =
      native_assets_manager->LookupNativeAsset(asset_id);
```

