To avoid unnecessary list copying and allocations when there are no registered texture frame callbacks, we can add an early return check if `_textureFrameAvailableCallbacks` is empty.

```dart
  void handleTextureFrameAvailable(int textureId) {
    if (_textureFrameAvailableCallbacks.isEmpty) {
      return;
    }
    // Iterate a copy so handlers may add/remove themselves mid-dispatch.
    for (final callback in List<ui.TextureFrameAvailableCallback>.of(
      _textureFrameAvailableCallbacks,
    )) {
      callback(textureId);
    }
  }
