![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

To ensure defensive programming and robust handling of potential edge cases, we should guarantee that `color_stops` is never empty even if `CreateGradientColors` returns an empty vector. Binding an empty storage buffer can cause crashes or validation errors on some graphics backends.

```suggestion
  std::vector<StopData> color_stops;
  if (params_.gradient) {
    color_stops =
        CreateGradientColors(params_.gradient->colors, params_.gradient->stops);
  }
  if (color_stops.empty()) {
    // The bound ColorData is required to be non-empty to be valid.
    color_stops.resize(1);
  }
```

