comment_body:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Instead of using a `late final` variable and assigning it inside the closure, you can directly assign the result of `_profile!.record` to `scene`. `Profile.record` returns the value returned by its callback, which makes the code cleaner and avoids the use of `late` variables.

```dart
          final Scene scene = _profile!.record('sceneBuildDuration', () {
            return sceneBuilder.build();
          }, reported: false);
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Suggest simplification and refactoring to enhance readability and maintainability. <sup>([link](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/master/.gemini/styleguide.md))</sup>
</details>

