![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

To prevent potential runtime `ReferenceError` or `TypeError` in non-browser, server-side rendering (SSR), or headless test environments where `navigator` or `navigator.userAgent` might be undefined, it is safer to guard these accesses defensively.

```suggestion
const getFirefoxVersion = () => {
  if (typeof navigator === "undefined" || !navigator.userAgent) {
    return -1;
  }
  const match = navigator.userAgent.match(/firefox\/(\d+)/i);
  return match ? parseInt(match[1], 10) : -1;
}

const supportsDart2Wasm = () => {
  const userAgent = typeof navigator !== "undefined" && navigator.userAgent ? navigator.userAgent.toLowerCase() : "";
  const isFirefox = userAgent.includes('firefox');
  if (isFirefox && getFirefoxVersion() < 147) return false;
```

